# Pairs with NewbornPinEventuallyUsable, and reproduces issue #5572's production
# shape: a live write never advances the leaf's read position, so a leaf born
# holding live writes keeps its block pin until a replay is scheduled - which the
# protocol cannot rely on for it - and its tree's WAL is retained meanwhile.
MODULE: NewbornPinEventuallyUsableNoLiveAdvance
TARGET: NewbornPinEventuallyUsable
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: live writes never advance the read position
PERTURBS: LiveAdvance

--- FIND
    /\ own[l] # {}
    /\ OwnUnapplied(l) = {}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no live advance.
    /\ FALSE
    /\ OwnUnapplied(l) = {}
--- END
